1
00:00:00,340 --> 00:00:02,560
Is kanji really necessary?

2
00:00:02,580 --> 00:00:04,000
What if Japanese used only

3
00:00:04,020 --> 00:00:05,760
hiragana and katakana?

4
00:00:05,780 --> 00:00:07,190
Look at this sentence.

5
00:00:07,230 --> 00:00:09,020
Haha wa hana ga suki.

6
00:00:09,190 --> 00:00:11,820
It means, "Mother likes flowers."

7
00:00:11,910 --> 00:00:13,610
Now, let's remove the kanji,

8
00:00:13,630 --> 00:00:15,660
and write everything in hiragana.

9
00:00:15,820 --> 00:00:20,120
Ha ha ha ha na ga su ki…?

10
00:00:20,770 --> 00:00:21,790
Wait...

11
00:00:21,810 --> 00:00:22,830
why does this suddenly

12
00:00:22,850 --> 00:00:24,440
look so confusing?

13
00:00:24,610 --> 00:00:25,790
Japanese has many

14
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:27,390
words that sound alike.

15
00:00:27,410 --> 00:00:29,310
Without kanji, readers may need

16
00:00:29,330 --> 00:00:31,070
more context to figure out which

17
00:00:31,090 --> 00:00:32,910
words and meanings are intended.

18
00:00:32,930 --> 00:00:34,830
Kanji gives your eyes an important

19
00:00:34,850 --> 00:00:36,510
clue, helping you recognize

20
00:00:36,530 --> 00:00:38,440
meaningful words more easily.

21
00:00:38,530 --> 00:00:39,880
Here's another example.

22
00:00:39,960 --> 00:00:43,020
Niwa ni wa niwa niwatori ga iru.

23
00:00:43,290 --> 00:00:45,040
Now look at it with kanji.

24
00:00:45,160 --> 00:00:48,220
Niwa ni wa niwa niwatori ga iru.

25
00:00:48,530 --> 00:00:49,630
"There are two chickens

26
00:00:49,650 --> 00:00:50,680
in the garden."

27
00:00:50,770 --> 00:00:51,870
See how the kanji helps

28
00:00:51,890 --> 00:00:53,390
make the meaning clearer?

29
00:00:53,410 --> 00:00:55,960
So, is kanji really necessary?

30
00:00:56,050 --> 00:00:57,750
Japanese can be written without

31
00:00:57,770 --> 00:00:59,470
kanji in some situations.

32
00:00:59,490 --> 00:01:01,150
But kanji helps make many

33
00:01:01,170 --> 00:01:02,710
everyday sentences easier

34
00:01:02,730 --> 00:01:04,390
to distinguish and read.

35
00:01:04,410 --> 00:01:07,070
Hiragana, katakana, and kanji each

36
00:01:07,090 --> 00:01:08,990
have their own important role.

37
00:01:09,010 --> 00:01:10,910
So, don't look at kanji as just

38
00:01:10,930 --> 00:01:12,750
another obstacle to overcome.

39
00:01:12,770 --> 00:01:13,990
Every character you learn

40
00:01:14,010 --> 00:01:15,510
helps you understand a little

41
00:01:15,530 --> 00:01:17,310
more of the Japanese language.

42
00:01:17,330 --> 00:01:18,790
Don't fear kanji.

43
00:01:18,810 --> 00:01:19,550
Learn to see the

44
00:01:19,570 --> 00:01:20,710
meaning behind it.

45
00:01:20,730 --> 00:01:22,070
Follow me, and let's

46
00:01:22,090 --> 00:01:23,800
master Japanese together!

47
00:01:23,940 --> 00:01:24,900
Mata ne!
